course: dictionary
lesson: 6384
title: Multicultural
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Multicultural means having or including people from many different cultures, countries, religions or backgrounds. Look at the word's parts: multi means many, and cultural is about the ways of life, customs and traditions of a group of people.
explain: Multicultural can also describe something that shows or celebrates many cultures. The words around it give the clue: «a multicultural festival» is a festival with food, music and dances from many countries. Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence, then swap your meaning in to check.
explain: Context helps again. «In Multicultural London English, "man" can mean "I".» The capital letters show that this is the name of a way of speaking, and the sentence tells you it belongs to London, where people of many backgrounds live together.
fact: Multicultural means having or including people from many different cultures, countries, religions or backgrounds.
fact: «Multicultural» can also mean showing or celebrating many cultures, as in «a multicultural festival».
fact: A place such as «a multicultural society» is one where people of many backgrounds live and work together.
fact: Multicultural London English is a way of speaking in London; in it, «man» can mean «I».
fact: The UK, Canada and Australia are countries where many people of different backgrounds live together.
exercise: What does multicultural mean? | Having only one language and one religion | *Having people from many different cultures and backgrounds | Full of loud music only | Very old and quiet
exercise: «We went to a multicultural festival with food from many countries.» What does this show? | Only one country's food | A school closed for the day | *Many cultures being celebrated together
exercise: Which phrase describes a school where children come from many different backgrounds? | A curt reply | A barely there whisper | *A multicultural school | An ancient castle
test: Which phrase means a society where people of many cultures live together? | A treacherous path | A quiet village | A glum farmyard | *A multicultural society
test: «Multicultural» means having people from many different cultures. Which word is closest in meaning? | Famished | *Diverse | Drooped | Barely
exam: In «Multicultural London English», what can "man" mean? | *I | Very old | Dangerous | Man, as in a male adult
